package com.grabthesevehicles.app;

final class AppPrivacy {
    private AppPrivacy() {}
    static final String TEXT = "grab these vehicles stores your interval settings, enabled state, latest request, and message rotation on your device. It does not collect or send personal data, and contains no ads, analytics, sign-in, or internet permission.\n\n"
        + "Notifications are handled by Android. Tapping a notification or the last-request card copies that message to your system clipboard, where you can paste it into another app.\n\n"
        + "The bundled notification sound is made readable to Android's sound player. This exposes only that sound, not your messages or settings.\n\n"
        + "Call settings and imported voice recordings stay on your device. With Contacts permission, native-call setup creates GTA caller names, pictures, reserved fictional 555 numbers, and the supplied ringtone in a separate local GTA Callers account. Only this app's caller contacts are queried or changed; they do not merge with your personal contacts. The account has no login or synchronization. Use Remove GTA caller contacts to remove it.\n\n"
        + "Your existing Phone app displays and controls these simulated calls and may save them in its own call history. This app never records your microphone or places a real phone call. Android manages call volume and audio routing. The ringtone is readable only as audio through the sound provider.\n\n"
        + "Clear app storage to remove settings and imported recordings. Removing the caller account or uninstalling removes its GTA contacts; Phone app call history is managed separately. Device backup or transfer features are controlled by your phone.\n\n"
        + "For privacy questions, use the developer contact details on this app's Google Play listing, when published.\n\n"
        + "This is an unofficial fan app and is not affiliated with Rockstar Games or Take-Two Interactive.";
}
